cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this framework or its test doctrine, please cite it."
title: "proven-tests-and-benches: tests that carry their own evidence"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jewell
    given-names: Jonathan D.A.
    email: jonathan.jewell@open.ac.uk
repository-code: "https://github.com/hyperpolymath/proven-tests-and-benches"
license: MPL-2.0
keywords:
  - evidence-carrying-tests
  - provenance-tiers
  - test-taxonomy
  - idris2
  - dependent-types
abstract: >-
  An Idris2 testing framework in which a test's warrant — the strength of
  evidence behind it — is a first-class, machine-checked value across three
  provenance tiers (Actually-Proven / Provisionally-Proven / Unproven), with
  coverage derived from executed tests at typed coordinates rather than
  declared, and a harness/payload doctrine under which the harness must never
  trigger and the payload must always trigger for its declared defect class.
